00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:21.860
Leveling up in the system, right?

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:23.680
I had been broken and

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:27.750
So I bought that what they were selling and so I became what they called a helper

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:32.100
It was a tragic experience where these people tried to commit suicide right in front of me

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:35.760
And I had to kind of save them and there was no medical attention

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:38.789
I was programmed to do these things rights

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:42.790
They conditioned me to have these responses, but I still regret them.

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:43.950
[CALVIN] You still regret it.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:47.249
I think that's kind of how I feel a little bit because

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:56.700
The things that I usually don't like the word regret because I don't think it it's productive to be so stuck in the past

00:12:57.400 --> 00:13:04.260
but the things the the negative feelings that came up in me what made me come over here to agree is

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:07.500
There were things that I was complicit to

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:12.270
That I witnessed that I thought was the right thing

00:13:12.339 --> 00:13:17.069
But there was something inside of me in those moments that I was like

